                <pb facs="0481" n="377" sameAs="frus:frus1932v03/pg377"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/4277: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China (Johnson) to the Secretary of
                            State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-02-18T18:00:00+08:00">February 18, 1932—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 18—1:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>My February 17, midnight. Conference this morning lasted 2 hours and appears to
                    have ended in complete breakdown. According to Chinese sources the Japanese
                    demanded among other things the withdrawal of Chinese forces 20 kilometres
                    without promising any withdrawal of Japanese troops. Japanese are also said to
                    have demanded permanent dismantling of Woosung forts. They are reported to be
                    preparing to present written demands at 9 p.m. tonight which it is believed will
                    be in the nature of an ultimatum. Chinese consider the Japanese proposals of
                    this morning totally unacceptable and do not believe that they were submitted by
                    the Japanese in good faith with any expectancy that they would be accepted.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
